Integration design patterns:
  - Mainly 6 types
    - based on 6 behavior types

Remote process Invocation
1. Request and Reply
2. Fire and Forget


3. Batch data sychronization
4. Remote call-in
5. UI based update on data changes
6. Data visualization

1. Request & Reply
  E.g: Claim management system (Claim API); Waiting for external app to send response
  Inbound/Outbound : Outbound
  Best Sol: Call out from lightning flow; Callouts using external services (Swagger Schema); Button in LWC/Aura/VF Page; SOAP Api callout; Http Rest callout
  Sub optimal Sol: Apex batch; queueable apex; apex trigger (async call) (SOAP API or Http rest callout)
  Flow: Salesforce to external

2. Fire & Forget: Whenver the response is available, we are going to process
  Outbound
  Best Sol: Platform event
  Good sol: Outbound message; Outbound message with callback
  Sub optimal: Using button from UI, Apex batch; queueable apex; apex trigger (async call) (SOAP API or Http rest callout)
  Flow: Salesforce to external

3. Batch data synchronization
    Outbound & Inbound
    Outbound: Best: Enable CDC || Good: ETL ;; Suboptimal sol: Remote process invocation || Flow: Salesforce to external
    Inbound: Best: ETL(Mulesoft/jitterbit/Talend/Informatica) || Sub-optimal sol: Remote call-in || Flow: External to salesforce
    
4. Remote Call-in  
  E.g.:  Node JS wants to send and get the data from salesforce
  Source system: External
  Inbound/outbound: Inbound
  Best Sol: 1. SOAP API 2. HTTP Rest API 3. Bulk API (Asyncronous)
  Sub optimal Sol: 1. Apex Web Service 2. Apex Rest Service
  Flow: External systme -> Salesforce

5. UI update based on data changes
  E.g: Salesforce updates to be shared with external systems
  Outbound & Inbound
  Outbound: Best: PubSub model/Platform event
  Inbound: Udpating the salesforce with updates in external systems: Best sol is PubSub or Platform events

6. Data virtualization
Outbound
Best: Salesforce connect
SubOptimal: 1. LWC/Aura/VF to display data by getting it from external system 2. Request & Reply

